Tark: search suggestions follow the default engine (spec §7).

Suggestions are on by default (ungoogled-chromium's inox 0006 turns them
off). A profile service, tark::SuggestRule, turns them off when the default
engine stops being Shodhya, and back on when Shodhya returns, but only
while the user has not set them: the pref tark.suggest_off_by_rule marks the
rule's own write, and any other change to search.suggest_enabled clears it.
Policy- or extension-controlled values are left alone.

